<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.2.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00386</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.2.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e778f4da-6b49-4d75-a39e-e6fdbf7b115e</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will write a system of equations from a table of values, graphs, and
        situations. You will also be able to graph systems by hand and use graphs of systems of
        equations to estimate real world solutions.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>Write a system of equations from tables of values and graphs.</item>
        <item>Graph systems of equations by hand.</item>
        <item>Estimate real-world solutions by graphing systems of equations.</item>
      </list>

      <para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>2.2.1: Interpreting Graphs of Systems of Equations</item>
        <item>2.2.2: Writing Systems of Equations from Tables
        <list id="list-00003">
          <item>2.2.2: Self Check</item>
          <item>2.2.2: Additional Resources</item>
        </list></item>
        <item>2.2.3: Graphs of Systems of Equations
        <list id="list-00004">
          <item>2.2.3: Self Check</item>
          <item>2.2.3: Additional Resources</item>
        </list></item>
        <item>2.2.4: Systems of Equations in the Real-World</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
      <list id="list-00005">
        <item>2.2.5: Practice</item>
        <item>2.2.6: Lesson Summary</item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>